  "what_this_does_not_show": [
    "The forecast-aware arm plans on the same hazard field it is scored against, so it carries NO forecast error: the margin here is what a PERFECT forecast buys over a present-perimeter policy, and this project's real model buys less by an amount this run does not measure.",
    "The buffer width is a free parameter and 1 km is the best of five widths tried on ONE fire, sitting on the crossing of two failure regimes; it is not a constant and an operator cannot know which width they are on.",
    "One region, one ignition, one departure time. The buffer band (250 m to 3 km) is a sensitivity check on this single run, not evidence that any width generalises to another fire.",
    "'Safe' is the committed definition (reached a refuge without standing on a cell at p >= p_cut when it was there), not survival."
  ]
